#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/code-signing-custom-builds.rst:7
msgid ""
"Code signing is an essential process for ensuring the authenticity and "
"integrity of your custom ``Mattermost`` builds. This guide provides steps"
" on how to code sign a build using your own certificates for Windows, "
"Mac, and Linux."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/code-signing-custom-builds.rst:11
msgid ""
"Make sure to follow each operating system's guidelines and best practices"
" for signing applications."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/code-signing-custom-builds.rst:14
msgid "Prerequisites"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/code-signing-custom-builds.rst:18
msgid ""
"**Code Signing Certificate**: Obtain a certificate from a Certificate "
"Authority (CA) or use a self-signed certificate if suitable."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/code-signing-custom-builds.rst:19
msgid "**SignTool**: Available as part of the Windows SDK."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/code-signing-custom-builds.rst:23
msgid "**GPG Key**: Create a GPG key if you don't have one."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/code-signing-custom-builds.rst:24
msgid ""
"**GnuPG**: Install `GnuPG <https://gnupg.org/howtos/card-"
"howto/en/ch02.html>`_ if not already installed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/code-signing-custom-builds.rst:28
